course: dictionary
lesson: 14796
title: Punctual: on time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Punctual means arriving or doing something at the time you agreed, not late. «Mia was punctual for the bus, so she did not miss her lesson.» Mia arrived when she should have, so punctual must mean on time.
explain: Look at the words around punctual for clues. Words like «registration», «timetable» and «the agreed time» tell you it is about time. Ask yourself: what time was agreed? Then swap in your meaning, «on time», and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Punctual is an adjective, so it can change to «more punctual» and «most punctual». Punctual is the opposite of late. A punctual person arrives on time, and a punctual train leaves and arrives when the timetable says it should.
fact: Punctual means arriving or doing something at the agreed time, not late.
fact: «Punctual to the minute» means exactly on time, with no delay at all.
fact: «A punctual train» is a train that leaves and arrives on time.
fact: Punctual is an adjective: punctual, more punctual, most punctual.
fact: Punctual is the opposite of late.
exercise: «Sam was punctual for school every day this term.» What does punctual mean here? | *On time, not late | Happy about school | Very tired | Always wearing a coat
exercise: Which word means the opposite of punctual? | Clean | Quick | Loud | *Late
exercise: «The punctual bus arrived at 8:15, exactly as the timetable said.» Find and copy the word that tells you the bus was on time. | arrived | timetable | *punctual | bus
test: Lily wrote, «Please be punctual for the trip tomorrow.» What is she asking people to do? | Bring a pet | *Arrive at the agreed time | Sleep in | Arrive late on purpose
test: Why might a school praise a pupil who is always punctual? | Because they wear the most colourful shoes | *Because they arrive on time for lessons | Because they never speak in class | Because they arrive at lunchtime
exam: «The train was punctual to the minute, so the passengers were not late.» What does «punctual to the minute» tell you? | Slightly confused | Very noisy | *Exactly on time | Very long
